# TLX ops/env.common.EXAMPLE — sanitized template (the live rig file is NOT
# published: it carries the ops admin token and the HMAC key).
#
# P8 multi-model layout: the wrapper (ops/engine_daemon.sh) sources env.common
# FIRST, then ops/env.canonical.d/<model>.env for the current model. The union
# of env.common + the dense model env is variable-identical to the pre-P8
# monolithic ops/env.canonical (config_fp unchanged; the monolithic file is
# retained as the pre-P8 rollback source).
#
# GENERATE your real file (one-time, on the engine host):
#   cd engine/ops
#   cp env.common.example env.common && chmod 600 env.common
#   TLX_TOK=$(openssl rand -base64 24); TLX_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
#   sed -i '' -e "s|REPLACE_WITH_openssl_rand_base64_24|$TLX_TOK|" \
#             -e "s|REPLACE_WITH_openssl_rand_hex_32|$TLX_KEY|" env.common
DEV=NV
M1A_SERVE=1
M1A_KEEPALIVE_S=10
M1A_GEN_REBUILD_EVERY=256
MTP_KERNARGS_MB=256
# L7 FIX 5: the global graph-submit budget (all graph classes incl. prefill
# chunk replays; gcycle.ParityGraph.submit counts, fence/entry rebuild resets).
TLX_GLOBAL_CYCLE_REBUILD_EVERY=928
# watchdog: max silent seconds on an GPU-owning RPC before clean-exit(1)
TLX_STEP_TIMEOUT_S=120
# engine-socket caps (V-24/V-31/V-30 stopgaps)
TLX_MAX_LINE_MB=4
TLX_SEND_TIMEOUT_S=10
# W5: P18 spill-law scoping (warn-only for the Tier-2 prefill families)
NV_SPILL_EXEMPT_NAMES=pf,p8
# ---- security (shared across models) ----
TLX_ADMIN_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_openssl_rand_base64_24
# R3-25: tokenizer-cache HMAC key (OUTSIDE the cache dir)
TLX_TOK_HMAC_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_openssl_rand_hex_32
